The rule taught is:

When two qualities of the same person or thing are compared, use “more + adjective” rather than forming the comparative with -er.

Example

❌ She is smarter than beautiful.

Here, we are comparing two qualities of the same person — she:

smart
beautiful

So according to this rule:

✅ She is more smart than beautiful.

Similarly:

❌ He is braver than wise.

✅ He is more brave than wise.

⭐ The important distinction
Same quality + different people/things

She is smarter than her sister. ✅

smart → smarter

Two different qualities + same person/thing

She is more smart than beautiful. ✅

more + adjective + than
